摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"The World's First Virtual Terminal for AI Agents","id":"gh:1231135337","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"mirage","slug":"strukto-ai/mirage","topics":["agent-sandbox","agent-tools","ai-agents","bash","claude-code","dsh-plugin","expressjs","fastapi","fuse","llm-agents","openai-agents","python","shell","ssh","terminal","typescript","vfs","virtual-filesystem","virtual-terminal"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"The World's First Virtual Terminal for AI Agents"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Mirage is **a Virtual Terminal for AI Agents**: one shell over data, CLIs and runtimes. Unix tools r"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"each every service, and `grep` runs on each service's own search, such as Gmail's or Slack's. Mirage"},{"id":"p2s3","text":" routes each command to the runtime that fits it, so most lines run in-process and only heavy work r"},{"id":"p2s4","text":"eaches a sandbox, which cuts infrastructure cost and tokens. The terminal itself is light: a workspa"},{"id":"p2s5","text":"ce takes **about 100 KB** of memory and each new session **about 10 KB**, so one process serves many"},{"id":"p2s6","text":" agents at once. Profiles decide what an agent can run and even what it can see, and scriptable poli"},{"id":"p2s7","text":"cies refuse anything those rules cannot express."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Here is an example of launching Mirage inside an application:"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"And what `alice` sees in the shell:"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## About"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Unified virtual terminal interface, not N SDKs and M MCPs.** Every backend speaks the same files"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ystem semantics, so pipelines compose across services.\n- **A virtual filesystem over every source.**"},{"id":"p8s3","text":" S3, Google Drive, Slack, Gmail, Redis and the rest mount side by side under one root, so an agent r"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"eaches all of them through a unified interface with the unix tools it already knows, like `ls`, `gre"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"p`, `find` and `jq`.\n- **Virtual command line tools (CLIs).** `git`, `slack` and `ntn` are answered "},{"id":"p8s6","text":"by Mirage itself, so an agent drives the service with nothing installed, across different runtimes a"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"nd machines, and one tool can be virtualized into two or more, each under its own name with its own "},{"id":"p8s8","text":"credentials.\n- **Routed, dynamic runtimes.** Python, JavaScript and any other command can be sent to"},{"id":"p8s9","text":" a configured runtime, in process, sandboxed or remote, which decouples computation from storage and"},{"id":"p8s10","text":" lets either change without touching the other.\n- **The virtualized Mirage shell.** It binds the fil"},{"id":"p8s11","text":"esystem, the CLIs and the runtimes into one command line, so pipes, redirection, variables, jobs and"},{"id":"p8s12","text":" history work across all three.\n- **Lightweight by design.** A workspace, the virtual terminal itsel"},{"id":"p8s13","text":"f, takes about 100 KB of memory and each new session about 10 KB, so one process serves many agents "},{"id":"p8s14","text":"without a container or VM per agent.\n- **Profiles designed for agents.** `allow`, `ask` and `deny` g"},{"id":"p8s15","text":"overn commands and CLIs, while `hide` and `show` govern files and folders, so a hidden path is not m"},{"id":"p8s16","text":"erely unreadable but absent from the filesystem the agent sees.\n- **A scriptable policy engine.** A "},{"id":"p8s17","text":"policy script can prohibit any dangerous action before it runs, and the same stack gates every VFS o"},{"id":"p8s18","text":"p and session write, so neither a file nor an environment variable leaks.\n- **Notifications wired in"},{"id":"p8s19","text":"to the VFS and agents.** External changes become an event stream on the mount, so a new Slack reply "},{"id":"p8s20","text":"surfaces as a change to the chat file in the virtual filesystem, and the agent reacts to it instead "},{"id":"p8s21","text":"of rescanning the tree."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Virtual Filesystem"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Everything Mirage \"mounts\" as one unified virtual filesystem for AI agents. Each\nservice sits side-b"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"y-side under a single root and answers the same POSIX semantics."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"|                                  | VFS                                                            "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s8","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s9","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s10","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s11","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s12","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p11s13","text":"                                                                                              [长行截断]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| **Object Storage**               |                                  |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Virtual Command Line Tool"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"These command line tools are virtualized: Mirage answers `git`, `slack` or `ntn`\nitself, so an agent"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" drives the service without that program being installed on the\nmachine. Each one mimics the real to"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ol, so an agent that knows the CLI needs nothing\nnew. Because they are virtual, the same tool can be"},{"id":"p14s4","text":" installed more than once under\ndifferent names, each with its own credentials, so every agent gets "},{"id":"p14s5","text":"exactly the\naccounts it is given."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"|                   | CLIs                                                                          "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p15s4","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p15s5","text":"                                                                                                    "},{"id":"p15s6","text":"                                                                         |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Virtual Runtime"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Runtimes are virtualized the same way, and not only for coding languages. Any\ncommand on the line ca"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"n be redirected to a configured runtime, so Python might\nrun in-process with Monty while\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"A profile decides what a session may run and what it may see. Commands are governed\nby customizable "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"`allow`, `ask` and `deny` rules, and paths by `hide` and `show`, so a\nhidden file is not merely unre"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"adable but absent from the filesystem the agent sees.\nFor anything those rules cannot express, a pro"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"file can name a policy script that runs\nat the gate on every command and answers allow, deny or ask "},{"id":"p20s5","text":"itself, though like every\nrule it can only restrict and never grant. Separately, a host can register"},{"id":"p20s6","text":" its own\npolicies on the policy engine, an\nordered stack the workspace consults on every command, VF"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"S op and session write. See\nthe policy docs."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
